      "title": "UK will miss climate targets if it weakens EV sales rules, advisers warn",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/18/uk-will-miss-climate-targets-if-weakens-rules-on-ev-sales-zev-ccc",
      "description": "<p>Analysts say mooted move to let more petrol and diesel vehicles be sold would wreck plan to reach net zero by 2050</p><p></p><p>Weakening the UK’s electric car sales rules would probably cause the government to miss legally binding climate targets, according to advisers tracking Britain’s progress to net zero.</p><p>The analysis by the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/committee-on-climate-change\">Climate Change Committee (CCC)</a> suggests the policy would blow a hole in the plan for achieving net zero carbon emissions by 2050 – prompting concerns that Andy Burnham’s government will have to slash the UK’s carbon emissions reduction targets, known as the carbon budgets.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/18/uk-will-miss-climate-targets-if-weakens-rules-on-ev-sales-zev-ccc\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-18T00:01:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Climate adviser urges UK government to ‘stand firm’ on electric vehicle targets",
      "link": "https://www.ft.com/content/52c034e5-ec65-4aa1-b693-77705c57ec23?syn-25a6b1a6=1",
      "description": "Climate Change Committee chair warns that watering down the ZEV mandate would put Britain’s green targets at risk and drive up costs for motorists",
      "source_name": "Financial Times World",
      "published": "2026-11-18T00:01:04"
